e-scale events</li> <li>Welcome students, provide clear guidance, and help ensure that their experiences run smoothly</li> <li>Coordinate event logistics, schedules, materials, communications, and other operational details</li> <li>Support Stripe’s existing education events and partnerships, including YSTE, UL ISE, Patch and IMT events</li> <li>Develop a thorough understanding of Stripe’s education initiatives and take ownership of increasingly complex responsibilities over time</li> </ul> <p><strong>Who you are</strong></p> <p>We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.</p> <h3><strong>Minimum requirements</strong></h3> <ul> <li>Experience coordinating events, programs, community activities, or comparable projects</li> <li>Ability to manage multiple workstreams, deadlines, and logistical details in a changing environment</li> <li>Clear and thoughtful written and verbal communication skills</li> <li>A welcoming and service-oriented approach to working with students, partners, and colleagues</li> <li>Ability to collaborate effectively with internal teams and external organisations</li> </ul> <p><strong>Preferred qualifications</strong></p> <ul> <li>Experience supporting education, student, early-career, or community programs</li> <li>Experience coordinating large-scale or multi-partner events</li> <li>Interest in learning about education partnerships and developing broader program-management responsibilities</li> </ul>",
