rganization.</li> <li>Coordinate cross-functional financial recommendations. Work closely with Product and Engineering, Pricing, Strategy and Operations, Treasury Finance, Accounting, and other Finance &amp; Strategy teams to support planning and forecasting activities.</li> <li>Own the financial planning and forecasting cycle. Lead annual budgeting, forecasting, and business reviews for Global Partnerships and Startup and Ecosystem Product areas.</li> <li>Guide operating expense management. Maintain visibility into resource plans, assess investment and efficiency trade-offs, and surface material changes that require leadership decisions.</li> <li>Partner on goals, metrics, and performance. Help leaders establish financial objectives and key business metrics for priority businesses and initiatives. Explain material deviations from plan, identify underlying drivers, and recommend actions.</li> <li>Build and develop a high-performing team. Coach and develop direct reports, set clear expectations, and maintain high standards for analytical quality, business partnership, and execution.</li> <li>Scale the team’s effectiveness. Improve financial models, reporting, planning processes, and analytical infrastructure. Use AI, automation, and better tooling to reduce manual work and create capacity for higher-value analysis.</li> </ul> <h2><strong>Who you are</strong></h2> <p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">We're looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.</span></p> <h3><strong>Minimum requirements</strong></h3> <ul> <li>15+ years in strategic finance, commercial finance, product finance, or FP&amp;A, with demonstrated success leading and developing finance teams.</li> <li>Strong commercial judgment and experience evaluating complex partnership agreements, building investment cases, and supporting negotiations through rigorous financial analysis.</li> <li>Strong grounding in budgeting, forecasting, headcount and operating expense planning, and business performance management.</li> <li>A proven ability to build trusted relationships with executives and cross-functional leaders, provide an objective perspective, and influence consequential decisions.</li> <li>Exceptional analytical and financial modeling capabilities, with the ability to connect detailed economics to broader business strategy.</li> <li>A hands-on leadership style and the judgment to prioritize across urgent transactions, recurring operating commitments, and longer-term strategic work.</li> <li>Excellent written and verbal communication skills, including experience presenting complex financial information and recommendations to senior leaders.</li> <li>Comfort working with large, complex datasets, a working knowledge of SQL, and the ability to create structure in an ambiguous, fast-moving environment.</li> </ul> <h3><strong>Preferred qualifications</strong></h3> <ul> <li>Experience at a high-growth payments company, fintech, or bank</li> <li>Deep understanding of payments unit economics, including card networks, banks, and the role of partnerships in enabling financial products.</li> <li>Prior experience in investment banking, private equity, or another transaction-oriented analytical role.</li> <li>Experience using AI, automation, and financial planning or analytics tools to improve the quality and scalability of finance work.</li> </ul>",
