      "description": "<h2><strong>Who we are</strong></h2> <h3><strong>About Stripe</strong></h3> <p>Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.</p> <h3><strong>About the team</strong></h3> <p>The Worldwide Alliances and Channels team develops and manages partnerships that help businesses adopt Stripe’s payments and financial infrastructure. These partnerships create new routes to customers, extend the reach of Stripe’s Sales teams, and help Stripe and its partners serve shared customers.</p> <p>The role sits on the Americas Alliances and Channels Tech Partnerships team. The team builds and executes joint go-to-market initiatives with major technology companies, with the goal of accelerating Stripe’s commercial growth.</p> <p>As part of this team, you’ll lead global partnerships across the artificial intelligence ecosystem, with an initial emphasis on leading AI labs. You’ll work across Sales, Marketing, Product, Solutions Architecture, and regional partnerships teams to develop shared opportunities and turn them into scalable global partner strategies.</p> <h2><strong>What you’ll do</strong></h2> <p>As a Partner Development Manager, you’ll define and build Stripe’s global partnerships across the artificial intelligence ecosystem, initially focusing on leading AI labs. Although the role sits on the Americas Alliances and Channels Tech Partnerships team, its mandate is global. You’ll establish relationships across partner organizations, develop shared value propositions, and translate early opportunities into joint commercial and product initiatives.</p> <p>This is an opportunity to build a new partnership motion from the ground up. You’ll start with focused opportunities, determine what works, and create a playbook that Stripe’s regional teams can apply around the world. Your work will span co-selling, co-marketing, and co-building.</p> <h3><strong>Responsibilities</strong></h3> <ul> <li>Build senior relationships across the commercial, partnerships, product, and technical organizations of Stripe’s priority AI partners</li> <li>Develop and execute global partner strategies, including shared value propositions, joint business plans, success measures, and operating cadences</li> <li>Identify and launch co-selling, co-marketing, and co-building initiatives that create value for Stripe, its partners, and shared customers</li> <li>Coordinate cross-functional teams across Sales, Marketing, Product, Solutions Architecture, Legal, Finance, and regional partnerships</li> <li>Work with Product and technical teams to identify opportunities for product collaboration and support productive technical conversations with partners</li> <li>Create repeatable partnership playbooks that regional teams can adapt for local markets and AI ecosystems</li> <li>Assess partnership performance, identify opportunities and risks, and communicate progress clearly to senior stakeholders</li> </ul> <h2><strong>Who you are</strong></h2> <p>We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.</p> <h3><strong>Minimum requirements</strong></h3> <ul> <li>8 or more years of experience in strategic partnerships, partner development, business development, or a related commercial role within technology or another complex business-to-bus…99337 tokens truncated…opportunities through the partner ecosystem.</li> <li>Partner with Sales to map relationships and introductions into strategic accounts and active opportunities.</li> <li>Create joint initiatives such as referrals, events, campaigns, content, and account-based activities that generate pipeline.</li> <li>Manage and grow a portfolio of strategic partners, ensuring partnerships deliver measurable commercial value.</li> <li>Share market, customer, and competitive intelligence to help improve our sales strategy and positioning.</li> </ul> <h3>What Success Looks Like</h3> <p>Success will be measured by commercial impact, including:</p> <ul> <li>Net-new leads and qualified opportunities sourced through partners.</li> <li>Enterprise pipeline and ACV influenced by partnerships.</li> <li>Competitor displacement opportunities generated.</li> <li>Strategic account introductions and partner-influenced opportunities.</li> <li>Partner-sourced and partner-influenced wins.</li> <li>Number and quality of active partner champions.</li> <li>Growth and productivity of priority partnerships.</li> </ul> <p>The goal is not to have the most partners but it is to have the right partners generating meaningful business impact.</p> <h3>What We’re Looking For</h3> <ul> <li>5+ years of experience in B2B SaaS, technology partnerships, business development, or channel sales.</li> <li>Proven ability to build partnerships that generate new business and pipeline.</li> <li>Strong understanding of enterprise sales and complex stakeholder environments.</li> <li>Excellent relationship-building, networking, influencing, and communication skills.</li> <li>Strong commercial mindset with a focus on measurable business outcomes.</li> <li>Ability to work closely with Sales and influence opportunities without owning the sales close.</li> <li>Proactive, entrepreneurial approach with the ability to build new partnership motions from the ground up.</li> <li>Experience in mobile advertising, adtech, martech, gaming, fintech, SaaS, or related technology ecosystems is a strong advantage.</li> </ul><div class=\"content-conclusion\"><div>&nbsp;</div> <div> <p>More details about our company culture and perks can be found on our&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.adjust.com/company/careers/\" target=\"_blank\">career page.</a></p> <p><strong>Interested? Let’s Talk!&nbsp;</strong></p> <p>&nbsp;</p> <hr></div> <div>&nbsp;</div> <div>We understand that <strong>imposter syndrome</strong> may sometimes hinder exceptional candidates from applying. So, don't hold back—apply with confidence! <strong>We're excited to hear from you and can't wait to chat!</strong></div> <div>&nbsp;</div> <div><hr></div> <div>&nbsp;</div> <div><strong>Equal opportunity employer</strong></div> <div><br>Adjust is proud to be an equal opportunity employer. We champion a diverse and inclusive culture in all of our offices around the globe. We understand that all candidates are individuals with unique backgrounds and talents. At Adjust, we assess candidates on qualifications, merit and business needs. We do not discriminate based upon race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, age, citizenship, marital status, disability, gender identity, veteran status or other applicable legally protected characteristics. If you see a position that excites you, please apply! We would love to have you join us in our mission to build a global tech company where we're all proud to belong to.</div> <div>&nbsp;</div> <div><hr></div> <div>&nbsp;</div> <div>To support an efficient and fair hiring process, we may use technology-assisted tools, including artificial intelligence (AI), to help identify and evaluate candidates. All hiring decisions are ultimately made by human reviewers.</div> <div>&nbsp;</div> <div><hr></div> <div>Please read our <a href=\"https://www.adjust.com/terms/candidate-privacy-policy\" target=\"_blank\">Candidate Privacy Policy</a> to learn more about how Adjust processes your personal information.&nbsp;</div> <div>&nbsp;</div></div>",
      "discovered_at": "2026-11-25T17:02:27Z"
    },
