      "description": "<div class=\"content-intro\"><p>Adjust, an AppLovin (NASDAQ: <a class=\"link\" href=\"https://www.streetinsider.com/stock_lookup.php?q=APP\" target=\"_blank\" data-tooltip-link-label=\"undefined\">APP</a>) company, is trusted by marketers around the world to measure and grow their apps across platforms, from mobile to CTV and beyond. Adjust works with companies at every stage of the app marketing journey, from fast-growing digital brands to brick-and-mortar companies launching their first apps. Adjust’s powerful measurement and analytics solutions provide visibility, insights and essential tools that drive better results.</p></div><div><strong>Make an Impact/ </strong>The role:<br><strong> </strong><br>As a Technical Account Manager, you will be part of the APAC TAM team based in Seoul, and work closely with several teams such as Sales and Integration, in addition to all other departments within Adjust. You are in charge of delivering exceptional customer experience to clients in Korea, SouthEast Asia and INSEA. This plays a major part in your goal to address client issues quickly and help resolve it effectively, maintaining their satisfaction and trust.<br><br><br><strong>Empower Your Potential/ </strong>Responsibilities:<br><strong> </strong></div> <ul> <li>Technical contact for your clients within Adjust.</li> <li>Support your clients on how to best use the Adjust product and help them resolve any technical challenges.</li> <li>Provide daily support and have check-in calls with your client base.</li> <li>Work with a global Support team.</li> <li>Serve as the trusted technical advisor to clients in Korea, SouthEast Asia and INSEA, ensuring optimal use of our measurement platform and services.</li> <li>Provide proactive account monitoring and technical health checks.</li> <li>Enable your client’s decision making and ensure they are set up for success by testing and validating their set-up.</li> <li>Troubleshoot complex issues by using internal