sales, participating in pipeline reviews, account planning, and quarterly business reviews</li> <li>Develop and execute joint business plans with strategic partners, including defined revenue targets, KPIs, and shared success metrics</li> <li>Build, activate, and grow partnerships in Mexico, spending meaningful time in-market with partners and prospects</li> <li>Drive cross-functional initiatives that increase pipeline generation, accelerate deal progression, and improve customer adoption through partner engagement</li> </ul> <p><strong>Partner Programs &amp; Operational Excellence</strong></p> <ul> <li>Partner with leadership to build scalable frameworks for partner engagement, including governance models, playbooks, and operating rhythms</li> <li>Lead joint marketing initiatives such as co-branded campaigns, field events, and demand generation programs with partners</li> <li>Ensure alignment across product, customer success, and operations to deliver a seamless partner and customer experience</li> <li>Standardize processes that improve consistency, predictability, and scalability of partner-led motions</li> </ul> <p><strong>Performance Management &amp; Strategic Insights</strong></p> <ul> <li>Track and analyze partnership performance across pipeline contribution, revenue impact, partner engagement, and execution effectiveness</li> <li>Identify risks, remove obstacles, and continuously optimize partner strategies to maximize outcomes</li> <li>Translate insights from partners and the field into actionable recommendations for product, GTM strategy, and customer experience improvements</li> </ul> <p><strong>Executive Engagement &amp; Market Representation</strong></p> <ul> <li>Serve as a key representative of the company within partner ecosystems, including executive briefings, industry events, and strategic planning sessions</li> <li>Build and maintain senior-level relationships with partner stakeholders to influence joint priorities and long-term growth</li> <li>Advocate for the company's vision and value proposition within strategic alliances and broader market conversations</li> </ul> <p><strong>Qualifications</strong></p> <ul> <li>8-12+ years of experience in partnerships, strategic alliances, channel, or ecosystem development within enterprise technology</li> <li>Proven success building OEM or embedded partnerships, including integrating technology into partners’ products</li> <li>Willingness and ability to travel up to 50%, including travel to Mexico as business needs dictate</li> <li>Proven success driving revenue through partner-led and co-sell motions</li> <li>Experience working within cloud ecosystems (e.g., AWS, Microsoft, Google Cloud), including co-selling, marketplace motions, and partner alignment</li> <li>Background in SaaS, industrial technology, manufacturing, IoT, or AI-driven solutions</li> <li>Demonstrated ability to build and scale strategic partnerships that deliver measurable, multi-quarter revenue impact</li> <li>Strong executive presence with experience influencing senior stakeholders internally and externally</li> <li>Deep cross-functional leadership skills, with the ability to align sales, marketing, product, and operations</li> <li>Program-building mindset with experience developing repeatable frameworks and scalable processes</li> <li>Analytical and data-driven approach to decision-making</li> <li>Ownership mentality with a bias toward action, accountability, and results</li> </ul> <p><strong>Nice to Have</strong></p> <ul> <li>Experience selling or building partnerships in the UK</li> <li>Professional fluency in Spanish</li> <li>Based in Texas or another city with convenient access to Mexico (e.g., San Antonio, Houston, Austin, Dallas)</li> </ul> <p>&nbsp;</p> <p>&nbsp;</p> <p><span data-ccp-props=\"{}\"><span data-ccp-props=\"{&quot;134233117&quot;:false,&quot;134233118&quot;:false,&quot;201341983&quot;:0,&quot;335551550&quot;:1,&quot;335551620&quot;:1,&quot;335559685&quot;:0,&quot;335559737&quot;